type: software
title: "hazardpulse: Unified Natural Hazard Prediction from Coherence Field Theory"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-03-11
url: "https://github.com/Jphilbrick10/hazardpulse"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jphilbrick10/hazardpulse"
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Philbrick
    given-names: Josh
    affiliation: Coherence Energy Labs
keywords:
  - earthquake prediction
  - hurricane rapid intensification
  - tornado prediction
  - coherence field theory
  - Helmholtz PDE
  - natural hazard forecasting
  - ensemble machine learning
abstract: >-
  Three natural hazard prediction systems derived from a single partial
  differential equation (Helmholtz coherence PDE). Earthquake prediction
  (AUC 0.894 on 1,051 M6+ events, exceeding ETAS by +0.144), hurricane
  rapid intensification (AUC 0.976, exceeding deep learning by +0.046),
  and tornado formation and severity (AUC 0.973 formation, 0.999 EF4+).
  All models are pure Python + NumPy with every algorithm implemented
  from scratch.
